[
    {
        "content": "<p>The docBlame linter triggers when <code>grind</code> (or <code>lia</code>, etc) is used inside a <code>def</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Init</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- foo -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lia</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/- The `docBlame` linter reports:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">DEFINITIONS ARE MISSING DOCUMENTATION STRINGS: -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">grind_3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> definition missing documentation string -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">lint</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 581731068,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1774478456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>With <code>lia -abstractProof</code> it makes <code>grind</code> avoid an extra def so it doesn't trigger, but this seems like it should be solved in the linter.</p>",
        "id": 581731192,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1774478551
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm hitting this in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37171\">#37171</a>, is it possible to fix in the linter?</p>",
        "id": 581731202,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1774478556
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In my eyes, the first branch should use <code>False.elim (by lia)</code> instead, and this satisfies the linter</p>",
        "id": 581731324,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1774478636
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, how does it fool the linter?</p>",
        "id": 581731673,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1774478821
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Since <code>lia</code> is being used to construct something of type <code>False</code>, instead of something of type <code>Nat</code>, and the former isn't required to have a docstring</p>",
        "id": 581732033,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1774479078
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Though, I think we do need another case in <code>isAutoDecl</code> in batteries to consider names of the form <code>foo.grind_3</code> to be automatically generated (just as we do with <code>proof_</code>)</p>",
        "id": 581732723,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774479501
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/pull/1733\">batteries#1733</a></p>",
        "id": 581733695,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774480051
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if we should have a better convention for autogenerated names, though (e.g. making sure they start with a <code>_</code>). I couldn't find any others on a quick glance, but we do have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Sat.Fmla.proof_of_subsumes#doc\">docs#Sat.Fmla.proof_of_subsumes</a>, which is considered to be autogenerated based on its name...</p>",
        "id": 581772695,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774480441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not familiar with Lean internals, but can't we have some attribute that signals it instead of a naming convention?</p>",
        "id": 581772817,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1774480519
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, we definitely could; this would be a more flexible solution, especially when we want names to remain user-accessible but still count as autogenerated. But adding any extension is a bit of performance overhead, whereas checking a name is cheap. <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span></p>",
        "id": 581773028,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774480658
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm, I'm still getting <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4-nightly-testing/actions/runs/23568806811/job/68626555732\">an unrelated error about leantar preventing mathlib CI</a></p>",
        "id": 581773525,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1774481015
    }
]